hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17951","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, Ali ibn Mudrik narrated to us, from Abu Amir al-Ashari, that a man of them was killed at Awtas, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, O Abu Amir, why did you not change. Then he recited this verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays harms you not when you are guided. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said, Where have you gone. It is only: O you who believe, he who strays among the disbelievers harms you not when you are guided."
"17952","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, The greatest misappropriation with Allah is a cubit of land. You find two men as neighbors in land or in a house, and one cuts off a cubit from the share of his companion. When he cuts it off, it is hung around him from seven earths until the Day of Resurrection."
